                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3486481947"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "should we mention that `wipe` this will (I assume) lose features like preserving cursor-position , etc.? `bufhidden=delete` or `bufhidden=unload` might be a reasonable compromise.\n\n(note: we absolutely shouldn't try to \"workaround\" users that want to wipe the buffers, because they are literally choosing to destroy the state that makes various features possible.)",
            "commit_id": "40894b1ce5769f9152676bcb3446031809a99faa",
            "created_at": "2026-06-27T17:39:46Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -65,6 +65,11 @@ These keys map to <Plug>(nvim-dir-open), <Plug>(nvim-dir-up), and\n \n The listing is read-only and does not modify the filesystem.\n \n+Directory buffers follow the global 'hidden' option by default. To wipe them\n+when they are no longer displayed: >vim\n+\tautocmd FileType directory setlocal bufhidden=wipe",
